{"id": "EUVD-2026-99260", "enisaUuid": "a6aeb2ff-d322-3377-a56a-82614173dc8f", "description": "QloApps through 1.7.0 contains a reflected cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows remote attackers to inject scripts through the price parameter of the back-office Additional Facilities form. Attackers can induce an authenticated back-office user to submit a crafted request whose unescaped price value is re-rendered after failing validation, executing JavaScript in the administrative session.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:31:01", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/SyMoELioMx", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/blob/v1.7.0/modules/hotelreservationsystem/views/templates/admin/room_type_global_demand/helpers/form/form.tpl#L208-L209", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/blob/v1.7.0/modules/hotelreservationsystem/controllers/admin/AdminRoomTypeGlobalDemand.php#L200-L232", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/pull/1809", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/qloapps-through-1.7.0-reflected-xss-via-additional-facility-price-field"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110219", "GHSA-v6h8-58w7-hfwh"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4dfd481d-5ff5-302e-ab23-782893205a51", "product": {"name": "QloApps", "vendor": {"name": "Webkul"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.7.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5090da71-2eea-37e0-a45d-1f61419ea8ce", "vendor": {"name": "Webkul"}}], "isExploited": false}